Subject: fix(cross-model): anchor the declared-outputs fallback to the last ## Outputs change (WFI-058)

prepare-panelist-input verifies each declared-outputs row against the working
tree and, for rows that legitimately drifted, falls back to verifying the
declared hash against the tree as of the "declaration commit". That commit was
defined as the last commit touching the implementation report FILE. The two
events coincide only until the report is edited for an unrelated reason after
its outputs have drifted.

Measured on epic-194 (2026-08-31): commit 8456b861 added machine-readable
`- Task ID:` header lines to three reports whose Outputs rows had already
drifted through the owner-approved apply chain. That two-line mechanical edit
moved the anchor past the drift, and the next bundle build fail-closed with
nine `declared output hash mismatch` lines on a tree that had produced valid
bundles the day before. The field workaround was to rewrite the frozen
reports' hash cells -- exactly the pressure the gate_report_declaration
channel exists to avoid at the evaluator layer.

This re-anchors the fallback to the last commit at which the report's
`## Outputs` SECTION itself changed, found by walking the report's history
newest-first while the section still fingerprints equal to the current one.
Row extraction is reused verbatim, so prose edits and header additions no
longer move the anchor while a real table edit still does. When no commit
carries the current section (the table itself is edited but uncommitted) the
historical file anchor is kept, so this can never lose the fallback entirely.
The stderr notice now names the anchor it chose.

Both runtimes change together. On the PowerShell side the report parser --
previously inlined in Invoke-DeclaredOutputsCompletenessCheck -- is lifted into
Get-PpiDeclaredOutputRows and shared with the new fingerprint, so the anchor
can never track a different row set than the authorization boundary reads.

Admits nothing new: every row is still re-hashed against the anchor commit's
tree, and a row that matches at neither the worktree nor the anchor still
fails.

Apply from the repository root:

    git apply --check docs/ci-staging/wfi-058-outputs-section-anchor.patch
    git apply docs/ci-staging/wfi-058-outputs-section-anchor.patch

